# Electronic energy levels for 11-species air
#
# For use with:  species air.species <sp1 sp2 ...> elecfile air.elec
#                collide_modify electronic discrete
#                fix <ID> elecmode
#
# format: species-ID N  temp1 relax1 degen1 spin1 dof1  ...  tempN relaxN degenN spinN dofN
#   temp  = state energy above the species ground state / kB (K)
#   relax = inverse electronic relaxation collision number (per-collision
#           relaxation probability under "collide_modify relax constant");
#           the 0.01 used here is a nominal default - calibrate to a
#           state-resolved kinetics dataset for quantitative excitation work
#   degen = total degeneracy of the level (sum of 2J+1 over grouped states)
#   spin  = spin-multiplicity class (2S+1) used by per-partner spin
#           conservation; for a grouped level it is the multiplicity of the
#           group's lowest state, so spin conservation across grouped levels
#           is approximate
#   dof   = unused (0)
#
# Level data: atoms (N, O, N+, O+) from the NIST Atomic Spectra Database /
# NIST Handbook of Basic Atomic Spectroscopic Data (Moore); molecules from
# Huber & Herzberg, "Constants of Diatomic Molecules" (1979), the source
# reproduced by the NIST Chemistry WebBook, cross-checked against Park (1990)
# and Gnoffo et al., NASA TP-2867 (1989).  E[K] = E[cm^-1] * 1.4387769.
#
# All bound states below the dissociation limit (molecules) or ionization
# limit (atoms) are included, with dense high-lying manifolds GROUPED:
#   degeneracy = sum over the group's states
#   energy     = the LOWEST state energy of the group (excitation is most
#                sensitive to the threshold, so grouping is conservative;
#                the grouped partition functions match the full NIST level
#                sets to ~1% up to 30000 K)
# Bound states slightly above a molecular dissociation limit that correlate
# to excited-atom products (e.g. N2 C3Pi_u, O2 B3Sigma_u-) are retained.
#
# The electron (e) carries no internal electronic ladder and is deliberately
# absent: its spin degeneracy (g = 2) enters the Saha equation for
# ionization equilibria, not the internal-energy relaxation model.
#
# Molecules ---------------------------------------------------------------
# N2:  X1Sg+ | A3Su+ | B3Pg+W3Du | B'3Su-+a'1Su-+a1Pg+w1Du | C3Pu
# O2:  X3Sg- | a1Dg | b1Sg+ | Herzberg c1Su-+A'3Du+A3Su+ | B3Su-
# NO:  X2Pi (both spin-orbit components, g=4) | a4Pi | A2S++B2Pi | b4S- | C2Pi+D2S+
# N2+: X2Sg+ | A2Pu | B2Su+ | D2Pg | C2Su+   (no grouping needed)
# O2+: X2Pg | a4Pu | A2Pu | b4Sg-            (no grouping needed)
# NO+: X1S+ | a3S+ | b3Pi+W3D | b'3S-+A'1S- | A1Pi

N2  5   0.0 0.01 1 1 0   72232.0 0.01 3 3 0   85778.0 0.01 12 3 0   95350.0 0.01 8 3 0   128248.0 0.01 6 3 0
O2  5   0.0 0.01 3 3 0   11392.0 0.01 2 1 0   18985.0 0.01 1 1 0   47562.0 0.01 10 1 0   71642.0 0.01 3 3 0
NO  5   0.0 0.01 4 2 0   55307.0 0.01 8 4 0   63257.0 0.01 6 2 0   68989.0 0.01 4 4 0   74998.0 0.01 6 2 0
N2+ 5   0.0 0.01 2 2 0   13190.0 0.01 4 2 0   36633.0 0.01 2 2 0   75993.0 0.01 4 2 0   92958.0 0.01 2 2 0
O2+ 4   0.0 0.01 4 2 0   47428.0 0.01 8 4 0   58514.0 0.01 4 2 0   70140.0 0.01 4 4 0
NO+ 5   0.0 0.01 1 1 0   75090.0 0.01 3 3 0   85233.0 0.01 12 3 0   92729.0 0.01 4 3 0   105709.0 0.01 2 1 0

# Atoms -------------------------------------------------------------------
# N:  4So | 2Do | 2Po | 3s4P+3s2P+2s2p4-4P | 3p manifold+(1D)3s2D | 4s+3d+Rydberg
# O:  3P (fine structure grouped, g=9) | 1D | 1S | 3s5So | 3s3So | 3p5P+3p3P | 4s+3d+Rydberg
# N+: 3P (grouped, g=9) | 1D | 1S | 5So | 3Do | 3Po+3So | 1Do+1Po+2p3s+Rydberg
# O+: 4So | 2Do | 2Po | 2s2p4-4P | 2s2p4-2D | 3s+2s2p4-2S/2P+Rydberg

N   6   0.0 0.01 4 4 0   27660.0 0.01 10 2 0   41493.0 0.01 6 2 0   119827.0 0.01 30 4 0   134643.0 0.01 64 2 0   149090.0 0.01 52 4 0
O   7   0.0 0.01 9 3 0   22830.0 0.01 5 1 0   48620.0 0.01 1 1 0   106136.0 0.01 5 5 0   110491.0 0.01 3 3 0   124635.0 0.01 24 5 0   137370.0 0.01 48 5 0
N+  7   0.0 0.01 9 3 0   22037.0 0.01 5 1 0   47032.0 0.01 1 1 0   67313.0 0.01 5 5 0   132708.0 0.01 15 3 0   157138.0 0.01 12 3 0   207454.0 0.01 20 1 0
O+  6   0.0 0.01 4 4 0   38574.0 0.01 10 2 0   58224.0 0.01 6 2 0   172419.0 0.01 12 4 0   238820.0 0.01 10 2 0   266512.0 0.01 26 4 0
